    "The finite-mode squared Hamiltonian includes its counterterm, and the Drude spectral density determines the stated retarded susceptibility with the correct cutoff factors.",
    "The complete matched-calorimeter protocol measures the temperature derivative of the combined-system energy minus the identical bare-bath energy. Full Gibbs equilibrium, fixed controls and subtraction before continuum limit fix the physical observable.",
    "The source differentiates exact local bare-oscillator energy rather than the specified calorimetric energy difference. This is a physical observable mismatch, not a defect in the FDT covariance mathematics.",
    "The oracle density Im[d(log susceptibility)/domega]/pi and the derivative of its inverse have the correct signs. The finite-bath reference independently builds physical couplings and the counterterm then subtracts bare mode heat capacities.",
    "Neutral instructions, fixed instrument uncertainty and no spectral-shift formula in the public apparatus preserve the implementation space. No unresolved scientific or public-input ambiguity found."
